.TH CLAUDE-DESKTOP-INSTALLER 1 "October 2026" "claude-desktop-installer 0.1.1"
.SH NAME
claude-desktop-installer \- verified official Claude Desktop application delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-desktop-installer install --assumeyes
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer update --assumeyes
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer release --json
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer prepare --directory DIR
.RB [ --app-version " VERSION"]
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer apply --deb FILE --sha256 HEX --app-version VERSION --assumeyes
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer status --json
.br
.B claude-desktop-installer uninstall --assumeyes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installing or upgrading the helper RPM queues a one-shot systemd job after
DNF finishes. The helper verifies Anthropic's signed repository metadata,
checks the package-selected SHA-256, extracts the official Linux Debian
package and creates desktop integration. It does not run Debian maintainer
scripts, add an APT repository, or disable the application sandbox.
COPR hosts only the helper. Anthropic does not support Fedora.
.PP
Check systemctl status claude-desktop-installer.service and
journalctl -u claude-desktop-installer.service for completion or failure.
The job retries failures, up to three starts in 15 minutes.
Reinstalling the RPM queues another attempt.
.PP
New helper releases select application updates. Claude Desktop on Linux
does not update itself. Cowork requires a paid plan and working virtualization;
the helper does not change user groups or firmware paths.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install, update
Require root and --assumeyes. Reconcile the package-selected release.
Reject foreign or changed files, metadata drift and downgrades.
Repair missing known desktop links from the retained verified package offline.
.TP
.B prepare
Download an official release into the requested existing directory without
installing it. With no version, select the newest version from Anthropic's
signed stable package index. Print the artifact metadata as JSON.
.TP
.B apply
Require root and explicit --deb, --sha256, --app-version and --assumeyes.
Verify the supplied package and ownership before replacing the bundle.
The caller approves the digest; this command does not fetch repository metadata.
.TP
.B release, status
Read-only JSON output. Release prints the packaged selection without network
access. Status verifies installation and ownership, including interrupted removal.
.TP
.B uninstall
Require root and --assumeyes. Remove only verified owned application files
and desktop integration. Preserve user configuration and other installations.
Retry interrupted removal; changed or foreign files block removal.
Final RPM removal invokes this command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/claude-desktop/
Verified Debian package, extracted application, launcher, desktop entry and receipt.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/claude-desktop
Application launch command.
.TP
.B /usr/local/share/applications/com.anthropic.Claude.desktop
Application menu entry and claude:// link handler.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates an invalid request, failed
verification, unsupported platform or incomplete operation.
